        "original_id": "f0e3cf86-23cd-5afc-9b2d-af4a7dd94bd5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hal McRae\n- Organizations: Kansas City Royals, Cincinnati Reds, Tampa Bay Devil Rays, Major League Baseball\n- Roles: left fielder, manager\n- Events: Kansas City Royals expansion founding, World Series appearances, 2002 Tampa Bay Devil Rays season\n\nFacts:\n- Hal McRae was born on July 10, 1945.\n- The Kansas City Royals were founded as a Major League Baseball expansion franchise in 1969.\n- Hal McRae played as a left fielder in Major League Baseball for the Cincinnati Reds in 1968 and from 1970 to 1972.\n- Hal McRae played as a left fielder in Major League Baseball for the Kansas City Royals from 1973 to 1987.\n- The Kansas City Royals lost the World Series in 1980.\n- The Kansas City Royals won the World Series in 1985.\n- The 2002 Tampa Bay Devil Rays were managed by Hal McRae in his first full and last season with the team.\n- The Kansas City Royals lost the World Series in 2014.\n- The Kansas City Royals won the World Series in 2015.\n- The Kansas City Royals have participated in four World Series.",
